From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:08:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a relay's Azure resource-mismatch 400 fails over and
 rests the failing relay (#5932)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A relay fronting Azure OpenAI that spreads one key over several
resources answers a conversation another of its resources began with
400 "The requested item was created under a different Azure OpenAI
resource." prevForeign knows the refusal, and passthrough asks once
more with the items magpie holds taken out; but when no repair is
available (Codex sends its own full history with store:false) or the
repaired ask is refused again, retryable did not include the refusal,
so a group stopped on it: the client got the 400, no other member was
asked, the failing relay took no rest, and the next request could pick
the same relay again (clhchan: eight group requests in five minutes,
each on the failing relay, no rest record, affinity why:"back" coming
back from the healthy spare).

Now retryable counts a recognized prevForeign refusal as retryable:
the next candidate answers before any reply reaches the client, and
the failing candidate takes its normal error rest, capped by its
rest-cap as any failure. A successful repair still returns normally
and rests nobody, and an ordinary input-validation 400 still reaches
the client without failover: the words of this refusal, and no word
list retryable matches, overlap.

From the reporter's own local patch on v0.1.3545 (five lines in
retryable, this classification reused whole), reworked onto the
current shape of the switch — the reporter holds the diagnosis, the
reproduction and the live Windows verification (routing log: newapi
400 rest.by:"backoff", api 200; the next route on api alone).

Run:
- TestAzureResourceMismatchFailsOverAndRests: a Codex-style
  store:false full-history request and a stored-history one whose
  repair is refused again both end 200 on the spare, the failing try
  carries rest.by:"backoff" with the original error in it, and the
  next group request skips the resting relay (red before the change:
  client 400, spare called zero times, relay once without stored
  history and three times with the first turn and failed repair in).
- TestAzureResourceMismatchLeavesOtherBadRequestsAlone: a
  `messages: field required` 400 reaches the client, one try, no rest.
- TestPreviousResponse*, TestUnknownPreviousResponseRelayedAsSent,
  TestNoFallbackForOtherErrors, TestRestCapOr, TestRestCapOff,
  TestOneRequestDoesNotClimbTheBackoff: green.
- Ablation: the prevForeign case taken out of retryable made both
  resource-mismatch cases red again; restored, green.
- Sibling scan: prevForeign is written nowhere else; its other reader,
  the passthrough repair, is untouched. retryable's other readers take
  the refusal the same way now: decideFailed rests a System One
  candidate for it, a stream error frame naming it falls to
  lateRests (refusedWords does not match it), an eventError after
  thinking began hands the turn over, a held error lets another
  provider answer, and draw and video try their next candidate —
  route-problem semantics everywhere, none touching the repair.
  6a253f8af..tip on fallback.go, prev_response.go and decide_group.go
  never touched retryable or prevForeign.
- Pre-existing red on this machine, parent commit too: TestMothX,
  TestProxyCheckSaysAProxyPassedBy. TestLaneLimitRoutes passes here
  with -tags nogui.

